149 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 119 0 R
/E (The global population is aging rapidly, and in India, the number of older adults is expected to reach 319 million by 2050, accounting for approximately 20% of the population. However, traditional elderly care systems face challenges due to their dependence on manual check-ins, scheduled visits, and emergency- based responses. These systems often fail to detect silent emergencies, rely on seniors being able to ask for help, and provide limited insights into gradual health deterioration. GenVoice Care addresses these challenges through an AI-powered voice monitoring system that enables natural daily conversations, identifies potential health concerns using rule-based keyword detection, tracks wellness trends with an 8- point scoring scale, and provides caregivers with real-time, color-coded alerts and comprehensive dashboards. The current version is a working cloud-deployed prototype designed for demonstration and research purposes.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
