228 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 125 0 R
/E (GenVoice Care uses a voice-based check-in system to monitor the well-being of older adults and share important updates with their caregivers. The system consists of three main components: Senior Mobile Application, Backend Conversation Service, and Caregiver Dashboard. Initially, the senior starts a check-in, and GenVoice asks questions about their mood, sleep quality, meals, social interactions, and need for assistance using speech recognition and text-to-speech technologies. The backend processes each response, identifies its intent, stores the conversation, and determines the next appropriate question. If the senior expresses sadness, loneliness, discomfort, or urgent symptoms, the system provides relevant follow-up questions or triggers an urgent- response procedure. At the end of the conversation, seniors can share additional information, which is recorded as a caregiver note and included in the final summary. The Caregiver Dashboard retrieves conversation details and automatically refreshes every three seconds, allowing caregivers to view recent messages, transcripts, and summaries. Thus, GenVoice Care provides an effective voice-based communication system that supports elderly wellness monitoring and keeps caregivers informed.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
